test/fixtures/legacy/gin-wire/
# Written by tools/linea.ts in one line per field (the forty ids on one line); tools/linea.test.ts
# compares the committed file to the tool's output, so the tool's text is the committed bytes.
web/shared/lib/cards/packs/linea.ts
# Written by tools/card-packs.ts in the same one-line-per-field shape from assets/cards/napoletane
# (docs/design/card-packs.md §5); `check` and the manifest test read it against the derived files.
web/shared/lib/cards/packs/napoletane.ts
# The shell's markup partials (docs/design/dry-round-2.md row G2): `{{slot}}` holes in gin's
# hand-owned layout, which tools/shell-markup.ts fills into each shell page and formats only where
# Prettier owns that page (this file decides); reflowing the partials would reflow gin's page.
# The renderer beside them (web/shared/markup/shell.ts) is formatted.
web/shared/markup/shell/
# Written by tools/parity/computed-styles.ts in its own compact layout (one screen per line, the
# value table inline) so a golden diff reads as a selector/property change; the tool's output is
# the committed bytes (docs/MIGRATION.md step 14).
test/fixtures/styles/*.json

# Deployed by hand with wrangler and outside the migration ("unchanged" in docs/ARCHITECTURE.md).
infra/turn-worker/

